From 715b5e70f586e14d2b16b0bfc1e437fcd88150bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:01:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] drm/gma500: add a parser for the SGX545 firmware file

Cedarview's SGX545 needs its microkernel and boot tables, which only ship
inside Intel's closed userspace driver. sgx545-fwcutter extracts them into a
single sgx545_ukernel.fw file. Add the code that validates that file and
produces the patched buffer images, register init scripts and metadata for a
given GPU address layout. Nothing calls it yet.

The parser does no allocation and has no kernel dependencies beyond types and
errno values, so the same source also builds in userspace, where it is checked
against the reference loader. Add a KUnit suite for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
